var e=`# Rule 25: Notice of Race, Sailing Instructions and Signals

**Part 3 — Conduct of a Race**

**Source:** Racing Rules of Sailing 2021-2024, World Sailing  
https://www.sailing.org/inside-world-sailing/rules-regulations/racingrules/

---

## 25.1

"The notice of race shall be made available to each boat that enters an event before she enters. The sailing instructions shall be made available to each boat before a race begins."

## 25.2

Signal meanings defined in Race Signals cannot be altered except under rule 86.1(b). Other signals must be explained in the notice of race or sailing instructions.

## 25.3

The race committee may substitute a flag with "a flag or other object of a similar appearance" when required to display visual signals.
`;export{e as default};